1
00:00:00,106 --> 00:00:02,446
(Sheldon:)How often have we had to leave
a movie theater...

2
00:00:02,609 --> 00:00:05,989
(Sheldon:)...because I got a headache
from drinking the Icee too fast?

3
00:00:06,238 --> 00:00:08,238
(Sheldon:)- I can't go.
- Then don't go.

4
00:00:08,406 --> 00:00:12,826
(Sheldon:)How can you say that? The scientific
opportunity of a lifetime presents itself...

5
00:00:12,994 --> 00:00:15,164
...my best friend says, "Don't go."

6
00:00:15,330 --> 00:00:18,370
- All right, then go.
- Listen to you.

7
00:00:20,502 --> 00:00:22,502
(Sheldon:)How can I possibly go?

8
00:00:22,671 --> 00:00:24,421
What are the words I can say now...

9
00:00:24,589 --> 00:00:27,259
(Leonard:)...to end this conversation
and let me go back to sleep?

10
00:00:27,759 --> 00:00:32,719
(Sheldon:)Odd. President Seibert posed
the exact same question.

11
00:00:34,057 --> 00:00:35,307
(Leonard:)How was it resolved?

12
00:00:35,475 --> 00:00:39,935
(Sheldon:)It wasn't. His wife set their dogs on me
and rendered the question moot.

13
00:00:41,773 --> 00:00:44,023
(Howard:)Just imagine. If he says yes...

14
00:00:44,192 --> 00:00:47,782
(Howard:)...we'll have an entire summer
without Sheldon.

15
00:00:48,738 --> 00:00:51,118
(Raj:)We could play outside.

16
00:00:52,325 --> 00:00:54,915
(Howard:)We could sit
on the left side of the couch.

17
00:00:55,078 --> 00:01:01,018
I could use the bathroom at 8:20.

